\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2.1.1}{\ignorespaces Effect of embedment length on the baseline specimen ($d_b = \SI {12}{\milli \metre }$, $f'_c = \SI {32}{\mega \pascal }$, $r_e = \SI {75}{\milli \metre }$). (a)~The predicted cracking load levels off by about \SI {100}{\milli \metre }, gaining only \SI {1.1}{\percent } over the remaining \SI {200}{\milli \metre }. (b)~The mean bond stress continues to fall as $1/L$, because a load that has stopped growing is being divided by a length that has not.}}{74}{figure.caption.77}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:factorL}{{6.2.1.1}{74}{Effect of embedment length on the baseline specimen ($d_b = \SI {12}{\milli \metre }$, $f'_c = \SI {32}{\mega \pascal }$, $r_e = \SI {75}{\milli \metre }$). (a)~The predicted cracking load levels off by about \SI {100}{\milli \metre }, gaining only \SI {1.1}{\percent } over the remaining \SI {200}{\milli \metre }. (b)~The mean bond stress continues to fall as $1/L$, because a load that has stopped growing is being divided by a length that has not}{figure.caption.77}{}}
